    "created_at": "2020-03-03T19:38:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-03-03T19:38:34Z",
    "body": "In practice, the only case where the promise is actually resolved in parallel is for `Blob`s. [`createImageBitmap()`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/imagebitmap-and-animations.html#dom-createimagebitmap) currently has quite a few cases with the following:\r\n\r\n> 1. Run this step in parallel:\r\n>\r\n>     1. Resolve _p_ with _imageBitmap_.\r\n\r\nwhich seems both wrong and unnecessary.\r\n\r\nIn Chrome, a [deprecated](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/master:third_party/blink/renderer/platform/scheduler/public/thread.h;l=118-123;drc=b892cf58e162a8f66cd76d7472f129fe0fb6a7d1) \"default\" task source that doesn't map to any task source in HTML in particular seems to be [used](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/master:third_party/blink/renderer/core/imagebitmap/image_bitmap_factories.cc;l=337-338;drc=b892cf58e162a8f66cd76d7472f129fe0fb6a7d1). Priority-wise it seems tantamount to DOM manipulation, history traversal, and a slew of [others](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/master:third_party/blink/renderer/platform/scheduler/main_thread/frame_scheduler_impl.cc;l=357-376;drc=b892cf58e162a8f66cd76d7472f129fe0fb6a7d1), but I don't think they are the exact same queue.\r\n\r\nIn Firefox, the [catch-all](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/91f6c02fcf4c16f78fdc4417f61f192688294066/xpcom/threads/TaskCategory.h#36-37) \"other\" task source is [used](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/91f6c02fcf4c16f78fdc4417f61f192688294066/dom/canvas/ImageBitmap.cpp#1173-1188). This seems to be equivalent to the DOM manipulation task source in HTML as well as many others.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
